;; ChromeOS-grade scorecard, version 1 -- the fixed measure behind "AIUEOS is N% of ChromeOS"
;; (Linear JUN-90, JUN-89, JUN-140).
;;
;; WHAT 100% IS. The sum of the weights of the REQUIRED rows is 100. A row counts, in full, only when
;; its :status is :pass at its :required-level, with evidence a person other than the author can
;; read back (a receipt, a log, a screenshot, a release artifact). Nothing counts in part. A row
;; nobody has verified is :unachieved, and that is the same as failed ("unverified = unachieved").
;; The score is the weight of the :pass rows over 100. Optional rows (weight 0) are listed, never
;; counted. Design text, code size, QEMU-only success and the old os-coverage marker share are not
;; product readiness and are not on this scale.
;;
;; EVIDENCE LEVELS, in order: :design < :qemu (a gate on QEMU/OVMF) < :device (the reference machine) <
;; :release (a signed release artifact, installed, on the reference machine) < :user (a person's
;; acceptance run). :required-level is the lowest level at which the row may be :pass. A QEMU run
;; never stands in for :device; a hosted run never stands in for either.
;;
;; THE :qemu-progress FIELD is NOT part of the score. It records where the QEMU-level work stands
;; (:pass / :partial / :none) so that progress is visible before any machine exists. It is shown
;; beside the score, never added to it.
;;
;; WHAT IS NOT FIXED BY THIS FILE: the reference machine's model and firmware, the ChromeOS device it
;; is compared with, and the exclusions. Those are the owner's to confirm (JUN-90 acceptance). Until
;; they are, the rows are fixed but the machine they run on is not, and no row can be :pass.
{:format :aiueos.scorecard/v1
 :date "2026-10-23"
 :issue ["JUN-90" "JUN-89" "JUN-140"]
 ;; 2026-10-23, owner: the reference is a VM on this Mac, and the ChromeOS it is compared with is the latest
 ;; ChromeOS in a VM on the same Mac. For the rest the owner said to go with the recommended choice: the VM is the
 ;; QEMU + UEFI stack the gates already run on this Mac (hypervisor and firmware recorded in each receipt); a run in
 ;; it with a kept receipt counts as :device-level evidence; no row is excluded (a row the VM cannot exercise stays
 ;; :unachieved, and :release rows still need the release artifact). The expected behaviours were taken from
 ;; ChromeOS and were not re-measured in a ChromeOS VM.
 :reference-machine {:target "VM on the owner's Mac" :model "MacBookPro18,4 (Apple M1 Max), the VM host"
                     :firmware "UEFI (OVMF) under QEMU, as the gates boot it"
                     :chromeos-device "latest ChromeOS in a VM on the same Mac (expected behaviours not yet re-measured there)"
                     :exclusions "none; rows a VM cannot exercise stay :unachieved"
                     :vm-counts-as-device true
                     :confirmed-by-owner true
                     :release-receipt-ok true}
 :levels [:design :qemu :device :release :user]
 :categories {
   :boot "Boot and first run"
   :identity "Identity and login"
   :shell "Desktop shell and windowing"
   :input "Input and text"
   :web "Browser and apps"
   :storage "Storage and network"
   :security "Security and data"
   :update "Update and recovery"
   :power "Power, hardware, accessibility"
  }
 :rows [
