   :needs "A receipt or log and a screenshot or readback at the required level, kept with the run."
   :status :pass :qemu-progress :pass
   :evidence ["receipt os/aiueos/qualification/receipts/vm-20261026/a2-display-change/receipt.edn"]
   :note "Measured 2026-10-26 on the reference VM (receipt, commit bf00936). Three fixes land together: the boot bind no longer demands exact equality with the reported scanout; the present no longer refuses a frame bigger than the REPORTED scanout, because QEMU bounds SET_SCANOUT against the resource and the host frontend scales the image; and the persistent desktop loop, whose idle branch halts, polls the display every idle turn instead of only on input. Two host resizes were seen and answered in one run -- 1280x800 -> 1200x1920 and 1200x1920 -> 1280x800 -- each with AIUEOS_GPU_DISPLAY_CHANGE_OK rebind-fullframe, geometry stable on every poll afterwards (no rebind oscillation), zero AIUEOS_EVIDENCE_STOP and zero AIUEOS_VIRTIO_GPU_FAIL, and QMP screendumps taken before and after (P6 1280x800, eight colours in a 40,000-sample scan, no black sample). The limits are in the ledger's rejection table: the desktop presents its OWN size and the host scales that image, which is not a re-layout at the new size; the second geometry came from this host's fullscreen mode because QEMU's cocoa window is not resizable unless zoom-to-fit is on (and zoom-to-fit shrinks the window on a QEMU-side feedback loop, measured 1280 -> 856 -> 361); the readback is the guest console screendump, not a host window screenshot."}
